{% icon id="trumpet-flag" size=32 /%}A live board for your alliance. Discord event alerts has three {% term id="plugin" %}plugins{% /term %}, each on its own tab of the {% term id="module" %}module{% /term %} page. Each one keeps a single Discord message up to date with what is open on the map.

{% terms_on_page /%}

- **Fortress** lists the {% term id="fortress" %}fortresses{% /term %} in Burning Sands, Everwinter Glacier and Fire Peaks.
- **Aquamarine Islands** lists the free islands in the {% term id="storm-islands" %}Storm Islands{% /term %}.
- **Aquamarine Towers** lists the towers in the Storm Islands that are open now.

## How the message stays up to date {% #how-it-works %}

1. When your bot signs in, each plugin searches the map around your castle in the {% term id="kingdom" %}kingdoms{% /term %} it covers.
2. It writes the list into one message in its channel.
3. Every few seconds, it updates the times in that message.
4. If the newest message in the channel is not from GGE Command, the plugin posts a new message and updates that one from then on. New messages arrive without a notification sound.

The plugins find the map spots one time, when the bot signs in. A spot that appears later shows up only after the bot signs in again.

{% aside type="tip" id="own-channel" %}
Give each plugin a channel of its own, where nobody else writes. Then the board stays one message, at the bottom of the channel.
{% /aside %}

## Fortress {% #fortress %}

The message lists each fortress with its kingdom, its coordinates and the time left. The list is sorted by time left. Everwinter Glacier shows at most 15 fortresses.

The plugin searches only the kingdoms where you have a castle. If you have no castle in Burning Sands, Everwinter Glacier or Fire Peaks, the plugin stops. The {% ui key="client:module.status" /%} card then says **This account has no castle in Burning Sands, Everwinter Glacier or Fire Peaks.**

{% settings plugin="fortress" /%}

## Aquamarine Islands {% #aqua-islands %}

The message lists each free island with its coordinates, whether it is big or small, and the time left until it opens. Islands that a player holds are left out.

The plugin needs the Storm Islands unlocked on your account. If they are locked, your {% term id="log" %}log{% /term %} shows **The Storm Islands aren't unlocked, so this plugin stays off.**

{% settings plugin="aquaIsland" /%}

## Aquamarine Towers {% #aqua-towers %}

The message lists each tower that is open now, with its coordinates, its level, whether it is Easy or Hard, and the hits left out of 10.

This plugin also needs the Storm Islands unlocked.

Both Storm Islands plugins search the map around your castle there. If you have no castle in the Storm Islands, the plugin stops. The {% ui key="client:module.status" /%} card then says **This account has no castle in the Storm Islands yet.** Restart the bot once you have one.

{% settings plugin="aquaTower" /%}

## Connect a Discord channel {% #channel-id %}

Each plugin has its own **Channel ID**. Paste the ID of the channel where its message should go, then save. The steps to find a {% term id="channel-id" %}channel ID{% /term %} are on [Discord attack alerts](/modules/discord-attacks/#channel-id).

## Tips and limits {% #tips %}

- The message updates only while your bot is online. While the bot is stopped, the times in the message stop changing.
- A Discord message holds about 2,000 characters. If the list is longer, the plugin cuts it at the end.
